# Sample cron job for cleaning up quarantined archived ngencerf job directories (production)
#
# NOTE: This file is a **sample only**. It is NOT installed directly.
# The production deployment script writes the actual cron entry to:
#
#     /etc/cron.d/ngencerf-cleanup-archived-pending-delete
#
# Because the real job lives in /etc/cron.d, the cron line must follow
# the /etc/cron.d format:
#
#     <schedule> <user> <command>
#
# The cleanup script is:
#     /ngencerf-app/ngencerf-server/cleanup_archived_pending_delete.py
#
# This script is used to delete quarantined directories created by the
# archive_jobs endpoint after a successful S3 archive.
#
# Archive behavior:
#   - job data is copied to S3 and verified
#   - the original active EFS directory is renamed to a quarantine path
#   - the endpoint immediately tries to delete the quarantined directory
#   - if NFS/EFS open-file behavior prevents full deletion (for example due to
#     lingering '.nfs*' files), the quarantined directory is left in place
#   - this cron job retries deletion of those quarantined directories later
#
# Quarantined directories are identified by names containing:
#
#     .__archived_pending_delete__.
#
# Behavior of the installed cron job:
#   - runs every 15 minutes
#   - scans under:
#         /ngencerf-app/data/ngen-cal-data/ngen-cal-work/run_calib
#   - retries deletion of quarantined directories using bounded retries
#   - does not require Django or database access
#
# The cron command only runs if the cleanup script exists.

*/15 * * * * root [ -f /ngencerf-app/ngencerf-server/cleanup_archived_pending_delete.py ] && /usr/bin/python3 -u /ngencerf-app/ngencerf-server/cleanup_archived_pending_delete.py /ngencerf-app/data/ngen-cal-data/ngen-cal-work/run_calib >> /ngencerf-app/logs/ngencerf-server/cleanup_archived_pending_delete_$(date +\%Y\%m\%d).log 2>&1